{%- comment -%}
  @param {object} product
  @param {string} [sizes]   - CSS width the card renders at, for the image's `sizes`.
                              Pass the real layout width; a fixed guess makes the browser
                              download a far larger file than the slot needs.
  @param {string} [loading] - 'lazy' (default) or 'eager' for above-the-fold cards
  @param {boolean} [mock]   - render from sample data (see mock-product) instead of a
                              product, so component previews work with an empty store
  @param {string} [mock_title]
  @param {number} [mock_price]
  @param {number} [mock_compare_at_price]
  @param {string} [mock_image]        - filename in assets
  @param {string} [mock_hover_image]  - filename in assets
  @param {string} [mock_badges]       - comma-separated badge labels
  @param {boolean} [mock_sold_out]
  @param {boolean} [mock_on_sale]
{%- endcomment -%}

{%-liquid
  assign card_image = product.images[0]
  assign card_hover_image = product.images[1]
  if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.image != blank
    assign card_image = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.image
  endif

  assign card_title = product.title
  assign card_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 1024px) 25vw, (min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw'
  assign card_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'

  comment
    Sample-data mode. Asset images go through the image snippet's `image` param and
    CDN images through `src`, so whichever is nil is simply ignored.
  endcomment
  assign card_image_asset = null
  assign card_hover_image_asset = null
  if mock
    assign card_title = mock_title
    assign card_image = null
    assign card_hover_image = null
    assign card_image_asset = mock_image
    assign card_hover_image_asset = mock_hover_image
  endif

  assign media_radius = ''
  if settings.card_border_radius
    assign media_radius = ' overflow-hidden rounded-[var(--base-border-radius)]'
  endif

  comment
    Aspect ratio: the class has to be a literal for Tailwind's scanner to emit it, so
    the setting maps to a fixed class here rather than being interpolated. `card_ratio`
    is the same shape passed to the image snippet, which crops the srcset to match.
  endcomment
  assign card_ratio = settings.card_aspect_ratio | default: '4/5'
  case card_ratio
    when '2/3'
      assign card_aspect_class = 'aspect-2/3'
    when '1/1'
      assign card_aspect_class = 'aspect-square'
    when '5/4'
      assign card_aspect_class = 'aspect-5/4'
    when '3/2'
      assign card_aspect_class = 'aspect-3/2'
    else
      assign card_ratio = '4/5'
      assign card_aspect_class = 'aspect-4/5'
  endcase

  assign card_title_class = settings.card_title_class | default: 'body'
  assign card_price_class = settings.card_price_class | default: 'body'

  comment
    Checkbox settings read as nil until saved once, so default-on has to be explicit.
  endcomment
  assign show_hover_image = true
  if settings.card_show_hover_image == false
    assign show_hover_image = false
  endif

  assign hover_effect = settings.card_hover_effect | default: 'none'
  assign text_over_image = false
  if settings.card_text_over_image
    assign text_over_image = true
  endif

  comment
    Scale has to clip, or the growing image escapes the card's box.
  endcomment
  assign media_class = card_aspect_class | append: ' relative block product-card__media' | append: media_radius
  if hover_effect == 'scale'
    assign media_class = media_class | append: ' product-card__media--scale overflow-hidden'
  endif

  comment
    Availability drives both the badge and whether quick add can appear. Sample data
    declares it, so the styleguide can show an in-stock card and a sold-out one.
  endcomment
  assign card_available = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available
  if mock
    assign card_available = true
    if mock_sold_out
      assign card_available = false
    endif
  endif

  comment
    On a collection page, link within the current collection so Shopify exposes
    the `collection` object on the product page. That lets breadcrumbs (visible +
    JSON-LD) reflect the path the shopper took. Canonical URL stays /products/x,
    so no duplicate-content risk. Elsewhere (home, search, related) keep the
    plain product URL — there's no meaningful collection context to carry.
  endcomment
  assign card_url = product.url
  if template.name == 'collection' and collection.handle
    assign card_url = product.url | within: collection
  endif
  if mock
    assign card_url = '#'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Tailwind safelist. Title/price classes arrive from Theme settings as strings, so the
  scanner can't see them at the point of use — listing them here keeps the utilities in
  the build: h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6 body-tiny body-small body body-medium body-large
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  data-product-id / data-product-handle are stable hooks so review/app widgets
  (app blocks or app embeds) can find each card and inject content like star ratings.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Captured so the same markup can sit over the image or beneath it — the only difference
  is where it's output and the wrapper's classes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture card_text -%}
  <h3 class="{{ card_title_class }} grow">
    <a href="{{ card_url }}" itemprop="url" class="{% unless text_over_image %}pt-3 {% endunless %}border-none block text-balance">
      <span itemprop="name" class="animate-underline">
        {{ card_title }}
      </span>
    </a>
  </h3>
  <div class="{{ card_price_class }}{% unless text_over_image %} pt-3{% endunless %}" id="cardPrice-{{ product.id }}" itemprop="offers" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Offer">
    <meta itemprop="price" content="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money_without_currency | remove: ',' }}">
    <meta itemprop="priceCurrency" content="{{ shop.currency }}">
    <link itemprop="availability" href="https://schema.org/{% if product.available %}InStock{% else %}OutOfStock{% endif %}">
    {% if mock %}
      {% render 'product-price', price: mock_price, compare_at_price: mock_compare_at_price %}
    {% else %}
      {% render 'product-price', item: product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{%- endcapture -%}

<article
  class="product-card flex flex-col group"
  style="--card-badge-padding-mobile: {{ settings.card_badge_padding_mobile | default: 12 }}px; --card-badge-padding-desktop: {{ settings.card_badge_padding_desktop | default: 16 }}px; --card-action-padding-mobile: {{ settings.card_action_padding_mobile | default: 12 }}px; --card-action-padding-desktop: {{ settings.card_action_padding_desktop | default: 16 }}px;"
  data-product-update="product-{{ product.id }}"
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  itemscope
  itemtype="https://schema.org/Product"
>
  <div class="relative">
    <a
      href="{{ card_url }}"
      class="{{ media_class }}"
      aria-label="View {{ card_title }}"
    >
      <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full p-(--card-badge-padding) z-3">
        {% render 'product-badges',
          product: product,
          badges: mock_badges,
          sold_out: mock_sold_out,
          on_sale: mock_on_sale
        %}
      </div>
      {% render 'image',
        src: card_image,
        image: card_image_asset,
        sizes: card_sizes,
        ratio: card_ratio,
        layout: 'cover',
        loading: card_loading,
        alt: card_title,
        class: 'z-1 relative'
      %}
      {%- assign hover_alt = card_title | append: ' - alternate view' -%}
      {% if show_hover_image and card_hover_image != blank or show_hover_image and card_hover_image_asset != blank %}
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-full z-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity">
          {% render 'image',
            src: card_hover_image,
            image: card_hover_image_asset,
            sizes: card_sizes,
            ratio: card_ratio,
            layout: 'cover',
            alt: hover_alt
          %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {%- if hover_effect == 'darken' or hover_effect == 'lighten' -%}
        <div class="product-card__tint product-card__tint--{{ hover_effect }}" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    {%- comment -%}
      Quick view trigger — hook only for now. A follow-up will open a modal using
      data-product-handle; until then this button is hidden unless enabled in
      Theme settings → Product Card.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% if settings.card_quick_action == 'quick_view' %}
      <button
        type="button"
        data-quick-view-trigger
        data-product-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
        aria-label="Quick view {{ card_title }}"
        class="button small absolute bottom-(--card-action-padding) left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-3 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 transition-opacity"
      >
        Quick view
      </button>
    {% endif %}

    {% comment %} {% if settings.card_quick_action == 'quick_add' and mock != true %} {% endcomment %}
    <add-to-cart-form
      class="absolute px-(--card-action-padding) left-0 right-0 bottom-0 z-3 overflow-hidden {% if card_available != true or settings.card_quick_action != 'quick_add' %}hidden{% else %}block{% endif %}"
    >
      {% render 'product-option-form',
        product: product,
        section_context: context,
        class: "p-gutter items-center bg-bg hidden",
        label_class: "text-center pb-1 block"
      %}
      <div class="pb-(--card-action-padding) group-hover:translate-y-0 translate-y-full transition-transform">
        {% render 'add-to-cart-button',
          class: "w-full",
          product: product,
          available: card_available
        %}
      </div>
    </add-to-cart-form>

    {%- if text_over_image -%}
      <div class="product-card__text-overlay absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-full z-3 flex justify-between gap-gutter p-(--card-badge-padding)">
        {{ card_text }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>



  {%- unless text_over_image -%}
    <div class="flex justify-between gap-gutter">
      {{ card_text }}
    </div>
  {%- endunless -%}
</article>
